  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $58.1M in FY2027 to date. The agency recorded 335 awards with an average award size of $173K. Obligations are down 99.9% year over year. Historical fiscal-year obligations show a sharp contrast: FY22 was $20.8B, FY23 was $23.9B, FY24 was $23.6B, FY25 was $28.3B, and FY26 was $73.3B, followed by the FY27 to date total of $58.1M. The largest spending categories so far in FY2027 are Custom Computer Programming Services at $37.2M, Office Administrative Services at $11.4M, and Computer Systems Design Services at $11.2M. The top vendors in FY2027 to date include METROIBR JV LLC at $22.7M, KYC ADVISORS LLC at $11.8M, and KONIAG BRILLIENT, LLC at $11.4M. The distribution of obligations in FY2027 to date is concentrated in a few software and professional services categories and a small group of prime contractors, reflecting the partial, fiscal-year-to-date nature of the total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest spending categories so far in FY2027?",
        "body": "Custom Computer Programming Services is the largest category at $37.2M. Office Administrative Services and Computer Systems Design Services follow at $11.4M and $11.2M, respectively. Other notable categories include All Other Support Services at $2.9M and Offices of Certified Public Accountants at $2.3M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors received the most obligations in FY2027?",
        "body": "METROIBR JV LLC received the largest obligations at $22.7M. KYC ADVISORS LLC and KONIAG BRILLIENT, LLC received $11.8M and $11.4M, respectively. Additional top recipients include SPATIAL FRONT INC at $6.5M and STELLA JV, LLC at $6M."
      }
